<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gabriel Dumont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837–1906</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gabriel Dumont was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a> buffalo hunter and leader who commanded the military forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a>'s Provisional Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a> of 1885. He won at Duck Lake and Fish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> but was defeated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batoche">Batoche</a> in May 1885, after which he fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and toured with Buffalo Bill's Wild West show.</p></div>
